🔍 Max Pooling is a stage after 'relu' to reduce the size of feature maps by using window only take the larges value in the window to combine it to make it a new feature map but smaller🔍

1) Apply Pooling to Condense
For for the last step in the sequence, apply maximum pooling using a 
 pooling window. You can copy this code to get started:

--image_condense = tf.nn.pool(
    input=image_detect,
    window_shape=____,
    pooling_type=____,
    strides=(2, 2),
    padding='SAME',
)--

image_condense=tf.nn.pool(
  input = image_detect, //➡️is the feature map after relu
  window_shape  = [2,2], //➡️sliding box
  pooling_type = 'MAX', //➡️take max value in each window
  strides = (2,2), //➡️ Move 2 pixels right ; Move 2 pixels down
  padding = 'SAME', //➡️This means TensorFlow will add padding (extra zeros) if needed so the output size stays clean.
)

