3)Global Average Pooling
A GlobalAvgPool2D layer is often used as an alternative to some or all of the hidden Dense layers in the head of the network, like so:

model = keras.Sequential([
    pretrained_base,
    layers.GlobalAvgPool2D(),
    layers.Dense(1, activation='sigmoid'),
])

------------------------------------------------

instead like this:
Flatten() → Dense(2048) → Dense(1024) → Dense(num_classes)
GlobalAvgPool2D:
GlobalAvgPool2D() → Dense(num_classes)
GlobalAvgPool2D = Take average of each feature map to reduce size.

➡️Used to make CNN models smaller, faster, and good for mobile apps (Flutter TFLite).
(2 + 4 + 6 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 1 + 2 + 3) / 9 = 3.67
In my words it only take the average instead of flatten all the neuron into 1D so much faster!

